{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0194Gk88ZobjYcz1c6w2eVdb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for every planned experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier definition. Let me go through each experiment systematically.\n\nLet me identify which experiments are \"planned\" (not yet done):\n- exp-014: Naturalistic validation (planned)\n- exp-028: Subsampling power curve (planned)\n\nWait, let me re-read. The user says \"对 experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验展开详细数据\". Let me check which experiments have status: planned.\n\nLooking at the experiment_plan:\n- exp-014: status: planned\n\n\n- exp-028: status: planned\n\nAnd there's also a what_if section with exp_026_arxiv_filtering_integrated (estimated_gpu_hours: 0.0).\n\nBut wait - the user says \"每个 planned 实验\". Some experiments are DONE but we need to predict what happens under \"best\" tier. Actually no, I think the user wants me to predict data for experiments that are status: planned, plus potentially generate imagined experiments.\n\nActually, re-reading the instruction more carefully: \"基于以上定义，对 experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验展开详细数据。每条预测都必须给出 result_rationale\"\n\nSo I need to predict detailed data for the planned experiments with rationales for each result.\n\nLooking at what needs predictions:\n1. exp-014 (Naturalistic validation) - status: planned\n2. exp-028 (Subsampling power curve) - status: planned\n\nAnd also the what_if experiment exp_026_arxiv_filtering_integrated.\n\nActually, I'm wondering if the user wants me to generate predictions for all experiments in the plan as \"imagined\" results under the best tier scenario, not just the ones marked as planned. The output format mentions \"imagined_experiments\" which suggests generating predictions for experiments that haven't been run yet.\n\nLet me focus on the planned status experiments first - exp-014 and exp-028 - and generate detailed predicted results with clear rationales for each. I'm laying out the predictions for the planned experiments under the best tier narrative: exp-014 should demonstrate that the depth classifier finds meaningful patterns in real web data with moderate correlation to quality signals, while exp-028 needs to show that K*=2 holds up robustly even at smaller sample sizes around 2000, proving practical utility. For the arxiv filtering integration, those results are already established from the prior experiment, so I'm thinking about what additional experiments might strengthen the overall story—perhaps validating on larger models, testing temporal stability, or exploring other domains. 每个 planned 实验\" which are the ones with status: planned. Let me focus on those.\n\nLet me write detailed predictions now.\n\nFor exp-014 (Naturalistic validation):\n- Apply depth classifier trained on controlled data to Common Crawl 2025/2026\n- Predict depth distribution of web text\n- Correlate with AlignScore and vocabulary richness\n- Expected: moderate negative correlation between predicted depth and text quality\n- Under \"best\": AlignScore correlation r ≈ -0.25 to -0.40 (negative because deeper = lower quality), vocabulary richness also negative correlation\n- Predicted depth distribution: majority predicted as depth 0-1, with ~15-25% at depth ≥2\n- This validates ecological relevance\n\nFor exp-028 (Subsampling power curve):\n- Test K*=2 determination at different sample sizes\n- Expected: K*=2 robustly detected at n≥2000\n- At smaller sample sizes around 1000, I'd expect roughly 60-70% of resamples to correctly identify K*=2, then climbing above 95% once we reach 3000+ samples, which directly addresses the reviewer's question about what minimum sample size we actually need.\n\nNow I'm ready to compose the YAML output. I should also consider whether to include the what_if entry—the user specified \"experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验\" and while what_if is technically separate, it strengthens the best tier narrative as an honest negative finding, so I'll include all three in the imagined_experiments list.\n\nFor exp-014 specifically, I'm working out the exact numbers: sampling 10K documents from Common Crawl snapshots from September 2025 and January 2026, with the depth prediction distribution showing roughly 62% at depth 0, 23%...\n\nGenerating YAML output... % depth 1, ~10% depth 2, ~4% depth 3, ~1% depth 4+\n- This aligns with estimates that ~30-40% of web text has some synthetic content\n- AlignScore correlation with predicted depth: Spearman ρ = -0.31 (p < 0.001)\n- Vocabulary richness (type-token ratio) correlation: Spearman ρ = -0.27 (p < 0.001)\n- Temporal trend: 2026-01 has higher predicted synthetic proportion than 2025-09 (+4.2pp)\n- Key rationale: the one-wash laundering effect means most recycled synthetic text is predicted as depth 1, consistent with K*=2 boundary — the classifier can't distinguish deeper from depth 2+, but can reliably flag depth 0 vs 1\n\nNow I'm looking at the power analysis for different sample sizes. The results show that I need around 1700 samples for 80% power and 2800 for 95% power, with the 5000-sample main experiments providing more than sufficient statistical power to detect the K*=2 boundary at θ=0.60.\n\nFor the arxiv filtering integration, I'm reconsidering how reviewers will interpret the null result showing that graduated filtering performs similarly to no filtering across metrics. The key insight that K* characterizes discriminability rather than utility might actually be framed as a positive contribution demonstrating scientific rigor rather than a negative finding.\n\nNow I'm organizing the output format with all the tables and figures for both experiments — the depth distribution and correlation matrices for exp-014, plus the power and CI width analyses for exp-028, along with their corresponding visualizations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49501,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49501},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5b9d37f-a5b9-4489-bce6-fa1fdb70397c","uuid":"d03d2c53-632c-4b76-979e-415e2ec472bf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0194Gk88ZobjYcz1c6w2eVdb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  best 档下，所有核心假设经受住审稿检验。exp-014 的 naturalistic validation 提供生态效度证据，\n  证明 K* 在真实 web 数据上有实际意义。exp-028 的 power analysis 回应样本量 concern，\n  证明 n=5K 的选择有充分 statistical justification。exp-026 integrated 的 honest negative\n  强化科学诚信叙事：K* 刻画的是 discriminability boundary 而非 data utility boundary，\n  这一 distinction 本身是 novel insight。审稿人将 honest reporting 视为加分项。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"exp-014: Naturalistic CC Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      对 Common Crawl 2025-09 和 2026-01 两个 snapshot 各采样 5K 文档，\n      用训练好的 15D OBD classifier 做 depth prediction，\n      与 AlignScore (factual consistency) 和 type-token ratio (vocabulary richness) 做 correlation。\n      验证 K* boundary 在 wild data 上的生态效度。\n    expected_results:\n      n_docs_per_snapshot: 5000\n      total_docs: 10000\n      depth_distribution_cc2025_09:\n        depth_0: 0.645\n        depth_1: 0.218\n        depth_2: 0.094\n        depth_3: 0.032\n        depth_4_plus: 0.011\n      depth_distribution_cc2026_01:\n        depth_0: 0.598\n        depth_1: 0.241\n        depth_2: 0.112\n        depth_3: 0.037\n        depth_4_plus: 0.012\n      synthetic_proportion_increase_2025_to_2026: \"+4.7pp\"\n      correlation_depth_vs_alignscore:\n        spearman_rho: -0.312\n        p_value: \"<0.001\"\n        direction: \"deeper predicted depth → lower factual consistency\"\n      correlation_depth_vs_ttr:\n        spearman_rho: -0.274\n        p_value: \"<0.001\"\n        direction: \"deeper predicted depth → lower vocabulary richness\"\n      correlation_depth_vs_perplexity_ref:\n        spearman_rho: -0.198\n        p_value: \"<0.001\"\n        direction: \"deeper predicted depth → lower reference perplexity (more predictable/generic)\"\n      binary_0v1_precision_estimated: 0.82\n      binary_0v1_recall_estimated: 0.78\n      depth_2plus_collapse_rate: 0.73\n      key_finding: >\n        Predicted depth 0 vs 1 separation is ecologically valid (correlates with independent quality proxies).\n        Depth ≥2 predictions collapse (consistent with K*=2 one-wash boundary).\n        2026-01 shows higher synthetic proportion than 2025-09, consistent with accelerating recursive contamination.\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下，naturalistic validation 成功但不过度。\n      (1) depth 0 vs 1 的 correlation 是 moderate (|ρ|~0.27-0.31) 而非 strong——这是合理的，\n      因为 AlignScore 和 TTR 只是 depth 的 noisy proxy，不是 ground truth depth。\n      审稿人不期望 wild data 上有 controlled experiment 级别的 correlation。\n      (2) depth ≥2 预测的高 collapse rate (73%) 完美呼应 K*=2 的 one-wash laundering 故事：\n      classifier 无法在 depth 2+ 之间做有意义区分，正是因为 depth signal 在 K*=2 处饱和。\n      这不是 classifier 的失败，而是 K* boundary 在 wild data 上的直接体现。\n      (3) 2025→2026 的 temporal trend (+4.7pp synthetic) 提供 policy relevance：\n      递归合成污染确实在加速。\n      (4) precision/recall 不需要很高（0.78-0.82 已足够），因为 this is not a detection paper——\n      目标是验证 depth signal 的生态效度，不是提出一个 production detector。\n      审稿人在 best 档下接受这些 moderate 数字为 \"consistent with controlled findings\" 而非 \"too weak\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Predicted Depth Distribution on Common Crawl Snapshots\"\n        content: |\n          | Predicted Depth | CC 2025-09 | CC 2026-01 | Δ |\n          |----------------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n          | 0 (human) | 64.5% | 59.8% | -4.7pp |\n          | 1 | 21.8% | 24.1% | +2.3pp |\n          | 2 | 9.4% | 11.2% | +1.8pp |\n          | 3 | 3.2% | 3.7% | +0.5pp |\n          | 4+ | 1.1% | 1.2% | +0.1pp |\n          | Total synthetic (≥1) | 35.5% | 40.2% | +4.7pp |\n      - name: \"Table: Correlation of Predicted Depth with Quality Proxies\"\n        content: |\n          | Quality Metric | Spearman ρ | 95% CI | p-value |\n          |---------------|-----------|---------|---------|\n          | AlignScore | -0.312 | [-0.341, -0.282] | <0.001 |\n          | Type-Token Ratio | -0.274 | [-0.304, -0.244] | <0.001 |\n          | Reference Perplexity | -0.198 | [-0.229, -0.167] | <0.001 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Stacked bar chart of predicted depth distribution, CC 2025-09 vs 2026-01. Visual emphasis on depth 0→1 transition dominating the synthetic fraction.\"\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot (predicted depth vs AlignScore) with marginal density. Shows clear separation between depth 0 and 1, but depth 2-4 cluster together — visualizing the K*=2 saturation boundary in wild data.\"\n      - \"Fig: Quality degradation curve — mean AlignScore and TTR by predicted depth. Sharp drop from depth 0 to 1, plateau from depth 2 onward. Annotate K*=2 saturation line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      naturalistic validation 完成两个目标：(1) depth signal 在 controlled 和 wild setting 间 transfer，\n      moderate correlation 充分（审稿人对 wild data 的期望本就低于 controlled）；\n      (2) depth ≥2 的 collapse 是 K*=2 one-wash laundering 的直接推论，\n      从 limitation 转化为 confirming evidence。temporal trend 增加 policy impact framing。\n      Limitation 段落诚实报告：无 ground truth depth annotation for CC data，\n      correlation 是 indirect evidence。best 档下审稿人接受此为 \"compelling supporting analysis\"。\n\n  - name: \"exp-028: Subsampling Power Curve\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-028\"\n    description: >\n      从 exp-001 (Pythia C4) 和 exp-017 (Qwen-cont C4) 的 30K 样本池中，\n      以 n∈{500, 1000, 1500, 2000, 2500, 3000, 4000, 5000} 做 10 次随机重采样，\n      每次计算 1v2 AUC 及 bootstrap CI，记录 K*=2 判定成功率（CI lower > θ=0.60）。\n      绘制 power curve，确定 80% 和 95% power 的最低样本量。\n    expected_results:\n      models_tested:\n        - Pythia-1.4B (1v2 AUC ≈ 0.6539, strong signal)\n        - Qwen-cont (1v2 AUC ≈ 0.6112, marginal signal)\n      resamples_per_n: 10\n      power_pythia:\n        n_500: 0.3\n        n_1000: 0.6\n        n_1500: 0.8\n        n_2000: 0.9\n        n_2500: 1.0\n        n_3000: 1.0\n        n_4000: 1.0\n        n_5000: 1.0\n      power_qwen_cont:\n        n_500: 0.1\n        n_1000: 0.3\n        n_1500: 0.4\n        n_2000: 0.6\n        n_2500: 0.7\n        n_3000: 0.8\n        n_4000: 0.9\n        n_5000: 1.0\n      ci_halfwidth_by_n:\n        n_500: 0.023\n        n_1000: 0.016\n        n_1500: 0.013\n        n_2000: 0.011\n        n_2500: 0.010\n        n_3000: 0.009\n        n_4000: 0.008\n        n_5000: 0.007\n      critical_n_80pct_power:\n        pythia: 1500\n        qwen_cont: 3000\n      critical_n_95pct_power:\n        pythia: 2000\n        qwen_cont: 4500\n      k_star_stability:\n        all_n_geq_2000_pythia_kstar_2: true\n        all_n_geq_4000_qwen_cont_kstar_2: true\n      key_finding: >\n        Pythia (strong signal) achieves 80% power at n=1500, 95% at n=2000.\n        Qwen-cont (marginal signal) needs n=3000 for 80%, n=4500 for 95%.\n        Our n=5000 design provides >95% power for all models including the most marginal.\n        CI half-width at n=5000 is ~0.007, sufficient to resolve AUC differences of 0.015+.\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下 power analysis 回应两个 reviewer concern：\n      (1) \"样本量够吗？\" → n=5000 对最强 signal (Pythia) 过饱和，对最弱 signal (Qwen-cont) 刚好充分。\n      这解释了为什么 Qwen-cont 的 CI lower=0.6015 如此边缘——它确实是 power-limited 的 marginal case，\n      但整体 7/8 的 evidence chain 不依赖这一个 configuration。\n      (2) \"最低需要多少样本？\" → n≥2000 对 moderate-to-strong signal 已足够，\n      这为 practitioner deployment 提供 actionable guidance。\n      CI half-width 的 1/√n 缩放与理论预期一致。\n      审稿人看到 power curve 后会认为实验设计是 well-powered 的，\n      Qwen-cont 的边缘性是 signal weakness（text-intrinsic）而非 design flaw。\n      这与 \"marginal case 不削弱整体结论\" 的核心辩护策略一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: K*=2 Detection Power by Sample Size\"\n        content: |\n          | n | Pythia (AUC≈0.654) | Qwen-cont (AUC≈0.611) | CI half-width |\n          |------|-------------------|----------------------|--------------|\n          | 500 | 3/10 (30%) | 1/10 (10%) | ±0.023 |\n          | 1000 | 6/10 (60%) | 3/10 (30%) | ±0.016 |\n          | 1500 | 8/10 (80%) | 4/10 (40%) | ±0.013 |\n          | 2000 | 9/10 (90%) | 6/10 (60%) | ±0.011 |\n          | 2500 | 10/10 (100%) | 7/10 (70%) | ±0.010 |\n          | 3000 | 10/10 (100%) | 8/10 (80%) | ±0.009 |\n          | 4000 | 10/10 (100%) | 9/10 (90%) | ±0.008 |\n          | 5000 | 10/10 (100%) | 10/10 (100%) | ±0.007 |\n      - name: \"Table: Critical Sample Sizes for K*=2 Determination\"\n        content: |\n          | Power Level | Pythia-1.4B | Qwen-cont | OLMo-1B (interpolated) |\n          |------------|------------|-----------|----------------------|\n          | 80% | ~1,500 | ~3,000 | ~2,000 |\n          | 95% | ~2,000 | ~4,500 | ~2,800 |\n          | 99% | ~3,000 | ~5,000+ | ~3,500 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Power curve — x-axis: sample size n, y-axis: fraction of resamples yielding K*=2. Two curves (Pythia solid, Qwen-cont dashed). Horizontal reference lines at 80% and 95%. Vertical drop-lines at critical n values. Shows our n=5000 is well above both 95% thresholds.\"\n      - \"Fig: CI half-width convergence — log-log plot of CI half-width vs n, with 1/√n reference line. Demonstrates that empirical convergence matches theoretical rate.\"\n    analysis: >\n      power analysis 将 Qwen-cont 的边缘性从 weakness 转化为 understood and quantified phenomenon：\n      AUC=0.611 距 θ=0.60 仅 0.011，需要 n≥3000 才能 robustly resolve。\n      我们的 n=5000 设计 provides adequate power，但 marginal signal 的存在本身\n      反映了 continuation mode 下 depth signal 确实更弱（vs rewrite 的 0.696）。\n      Power curve 同时为 practitioner 提供 deployment guidance：\n      如果只需要 binary detection (0v1)，n=500 即绰绰有余（AUC>0.92 everywhere）；\n      depth discrimination 的 power requirement 与 K* boundary 处的 signal strength 成正比。\n\n  - name: \"exp-026 arXiv Filtering Negative Result Integration\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_026_arxiv_filtering_integrated\"\n    description: >\n      将 exp-025 (Pythia filtering null) 和 exp-026 (arXiv graduated filtering null) 的负向结果\n      整合进论文 Section 5 和 Discussion。不产生新实验数据，但重新框架化已有结果，\n      引出 \"K* characterizes discriminability, not data utility\" 的核心洞察。\n    expected_results:\n      # 复用已有数据，无新实验\n      exp025_summary:\n        pythia_binary_vs_nofilter_mmlu_delta: \"+0.0017\"\n        pythia_binary_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_delta: \"+0.0000\"\n        pythia_graduated_vs_nofilter_mmlu_delta: \"-0.0007\"\n        conclusion: \"all deltas within noise (max 0.17pp)\"\n      exp026_summary:\n        arxiv_graduated_vs_nofilter_mmlu_delta: \"+0.0001\"\n        arxiv_graduated_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_delta: \"-0.0001\"\n        arxiv_binary_vs_nofilter_mmlu_delta: \"-0.0023\"\n        arxiv_binary_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_delta: \"+0.0042\"\n        conclusion: \"graduated ≈ no_filter; binary shows metric-specific trade-off\"\n      paper_framing:\n        section_5_addition: \"Table 5: arXiv Domain Filtering Results (K*=3)\"\n        discussion_insight: >\n          K* characterizes the statistical discriminability boundary of recursive generation depth,\n          not the downstream utility boundary. Depth 2 and 3 arXiv text is statistically distinguishable\n          (2v3 AUC=0.64) but not necessarily detrimental to training (graduated ≈ no_filter).\n          This distinction is practically important: K* tells curators WHERE detection can\n          differentiate depths, but not WHETHER differentiation improves outcomes.\n        honest_negative_framing: >\n          We hypothesized that arXiv K*=3 would enable graduated filtering to outperform binary.\n          This hypothesis was not confirmed. The null result reveals a fundamental distinction:\n          K* measures discriminability, not utility.\n      reviewer_reception_prediction:\n        credibility_boost: \"+0.3 to +0.5 ARR points on soundness/presentation\"\n        trivial_concern_reduction: \"honest reporting of disconfirmed hypothesis reduces suspicion of cherry-picking\"\n        insight_value: \"K* ≠ utility distinction is a genuine conceptual contribution\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下，honest negative 是科学诚信的 strong signal：\n      (1) 审稿人在 2024-2026 的 ML 生态中对 cherry-picking 高度警觉。\n      一篇主动报告 disconfirmed hypothesis 的论文立即与 \"只报好结果\" 的 median submission 区分开。\n      (2) K* ≠ utility 的洞察不是空洞的\"future work\"——它有具体的 empirical grounding：\n      arXiv 2v3 AUC=0.64 证明 depth 2-3 确实 statistically distinguishable，\n      但 downstream eval 显示 graduated filtering 无增量价值。\n      这意味着 depth 2-3 arXiv 文本虽然在 feature space 上可分，\n      但其质量差异不足以影响 LM training dynamics。\n      这一 gap 在 DPI framework 下是 coherent 的：\n      DPI 保证的是 information loss（features 可以检测到），但 information loss 未必 map 到 training utility loss。\n      (3) exp-025 Pythia null 进一步强化：即使在 C4 K*=2 上，\n      Pythia 这种较弱模型的 filtering 收益也在 noise level。\n      结合 exp-006 Qwen C4 上 binary 的显著优势，\n      论文的叙事变为 \"filtering 收益取决于 base model capacity × domain × contamination level 的交互\"，\n      而非 universal claim。这种 nuanced framing 在 best 档下被审稿人视为 scientific maturity。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5 (paper): arXiv Domain Filtering (K*=3) — Negative Result\"\n        content: |\n          | Strategy | MMLU | HellaSwag | Δ MMLU vs no-filter | Δ HS vs no-filter |\n          |----------|------|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|\n          | No filter | 0.5899±0.0008 | 0.6600±0.0002 | — | — |\n          | Binary | 0.5876±0.0004 | 0.6642±0.0004 | -0.23pp (p=0.005) | +0.42pp (p<0.001) |\n          | Graduated (α=0.9) | 0.5900±0.0011 | 0.6599±0.0003 | +0.01pp (p=0.89) | -0.01pp (p=0.71) |\n      - name: \"Discussion Table: K* vs Utility Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Domain | K* | Graduated > Binary? | Interpretation |\n          |--------|-----|-------------------|----------------|\n          | C4 (Qwen) | 2 | No (binary best) | K*=2 → binary sufficient, graduated adds noise |\n          | C4 (Pythia) | 2 | No (all ≈ equal) | Weaker model → filtering benefit below detection |\n          | arXiv (Qwen) | 3 | No (graduated ≈ no-filter) | K*=3 discriminability ≠ training utility |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig (Discussion): Conceptual diagram — two-axis plot with 'Statistical Discriminability (K*)' on x-axis and 'Downstream Utility Gain from Depth-Aware Filtering' on y-axis. Three domain points plotted: Wikipedia (K*=1, minimal gain), C4 (K*=2, moderate gain with binary), arXiv (K*=3, no gain from graduated). The non-monotonic relationship between K* and utility is the key visual message.\"\n    analysis: >\n      integration 的核心价值不在新数据，而在 reframing。\n      exp-025/exp-026 的 null results 在 naive framing 下削弱 C3 (\"K*-aware filtering works\")。\n      但在 best 档的 sophisticated framing 下，它们：\n      (1) 区分了 K* 的 diagnostic 功能（测量 discriminability boundary）与 prescriptive 功能（指导 curation），\n      (2) 为 C3 claim 增加 nuance：binary filtering 在 K*=2 web text 上有效是 C3 的 validated core，\n      graduated 在 K*=3 上无效是 honest boundary condition，\n      (3) 引出 \"K* ≠ utility\" 作为 Discussion 的独立贡献点，\n      potentially 激发 follow-up 研究（何时 depth discriminability DOES translate to utility？）。\n      审稿人在 best 档下认为这种自我修正式叙事 \"refreshing\" 且 \"scientifically mature\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49501,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49501},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5b9d37f-a5b9-4489-bce6-fa1fdb70397c","uuid":"833706a9-822c-4450-851a-6a5a202699e1"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":160472,"duration_api_ms":162105,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  best 档下，所有核心假设经受住审稿检验。exp-014 的 naturalistic validation 提供生态效度证据，\n  证明 K* 在真实 web 数据上有实际意义。exp-028 的 power analysis 回应样本量 concern，\n  证明 n=5K 的选择有充分 statistical justification。exp-026 integrated 的 honest negative\n  强化科学诚信叙事：K* 刻画的是 discriminability boundary 而非 data utility boundary，\n  这一 distinction 本身是 novel insight。审稿人将 honest reporting 视为加分项。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"exp-014: Naturalistic CC Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      对 Common Crawl 2025-09 和 2026-01 两个 snapshot 各采样 5K 文档，\n      用训练好的 15D OBD classifier 做 depth prediction，\n      与 AlignScore (factual consistency) 和 type-token ratio (vocabulary richness) 做 correlation。\n      验证 K* boundary 在 wild data 上的生态效度。\n    expected_results:\n      n_docs_per_snapshot: 5000\n      total_docs: 10000\n      depth_distribution_cc2025_09:\n        depth_0: 0.645\n        depth_1: 0.218\n        depth_2: 0.094\n        depth_3: 0.032\n        depth_4_plus: 0.011\n      depth_distribution_cc2026_01:\n        depth_0: 0.598\n        depth_1: 0.241\n        depth_2: 0.112\n        depth_3: 0.037\n        depth_4_plus: 0.012\n      synthetic_proportion_increase_2025_to_2026: \"+4.7pp\"\n      correlation_depth_vs_alignscore:\n        spearman_rho: -0.312\n        p_value: \"<0.001\"\n        direction: \"deeper predicted depth → lower factual consistency\"\n      correlation_depth_vs_ttr:\n        spearman_rho: -0.274\n        p_value: \"<0.001\"\n        direction: \"deeper predicted depth → lower vocabulary richness\"\n      correlation_depth_vs_perplexity_ref:\n        spearman_rho: -0.198\n        p_value: \"<0.001\"\n        direction: \"deeper predicted depth → lower reference perplexity (more predictable/generic)\"\n      binary_0v1_precision_estimated: 0.82\n      binary_0v1_recall_estimated: 0.78\n      depth_2plus_collapse_rate: 0.73\n      key_finding: >\n        Predicted depth 0 vs 1 separation is ecologically valid (correlates with independent quality proxies).\n        Depth ≥2 predictions collapse (consistent with K*=2 one-wash boundary).\n        2026-01 shows higher synthetic proportion than 2025-09, consistent with accelerating recursive contamination.\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下，naturalistic validation 成功但不过度。\n      (1) depth 0 vs 1 的 correlation 是 moderate (|ρ|~0.27-0.31) 而非 strong——这是合理的，\n      因为 AlignScore 和 TTR 只是 depth 的 noisy proxy，不是 ground truth depth。\n      审稿人不期望 wild data 上有 controlled experiment 级别的 correlation。\n      (2) depth ≥2 预测的高 collapse rate (73%) 完美呼应 K*=2 的 one-wash laundering 故事：\n      classifier 无法在 depth 2+ 之间做有意义区分，正是因为 depth signal 在 K*=2 处饱和。\n      这不是 classifier 的失败，而是 K* boundary 在 wild data 上的直接体现。\n      (3) 2025→2026 的 temporal trend (+4.7pp synthetic) 提供 policy relevance：\n      递归合成污染确实在加速。\n      (4) precision/recall 不需要很高（0.78-0.82 已足够），因为 this is not a detection paper——\n      目标是验证 depth signal 的生态效度，不是提出一个 production detector。\n      审稿人在 best 档下接受这些 moderate 数字为 \"consistent with controlled findings\" 而非 \"too weak\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Predicted Depth Distribution on Common Crawl Snapshots\"\n        content: |\n          | Predicted Depth | CC 2025-09 | CC 2026-01 | Δ |\n          |----------------|-----------|-----------|-------|\n          | 0 (human) | 64.5% | 59.8% | -4.7pp |\n          | 1 | 21.8% | 24.1% | +2.3pp |\n          | 2 | 9.4% | 11.2% | +1.8pp |\n          | 3 | 3.2% | 3.7% | +0.5pp |\n          | 4+ | 1.1% | 1.2% | +0.1pp |\n          | Total synthetic (≥1) | 35.5% | 40.2% | +4.7pp |\n      - name: \"Table: Correlation of Predicted Depth with Quality Proxies\"\n        content: |\n          | Quality Metric | Spearman ρ | 95% CI | p-value |\n          |---------------|-----------|---------|---------|\n          | AlignScore | -0.312 | [-0.341, -0.282] | <0.001 |\n          | Type-Token Ratio | -0.274 | [-0.304, -0.244] | <0.001 |\n          | Reference Perplexity | -0.198 | [-0.229, -0.167] | <0.001 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Stacked bar chart of predicted depth distribution, CC 2025-09 vs 2026-01. Visual emphasis on depth 0→1 transition dominating the synthetic fraction.\"\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot (predicted depth vs AlignScore) with marginal density. Shows clear separation between depth 0 and 1, but depth 2-4 cluster together — visualizing the K*=2 saturation boundary in wild data.\"\n      - \"Fig: Quality degradation curve — mean AlignScore and TTR by predicted depth. Sharp drop from depth 0 to 1, plateau from depth 2 onward. Annotate K*=2 saturation line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      naturalistic validation 完成两个目标：(1) depth signal 在 controlled 和 wild setting 间 transfer，\n      moderate correlation 充分（审稿人对 wild data 的期望本就低于 controlled）；\n      (2) depth ≥2 的 collapse 是 K*=2 one-wash laundering 的直接推论，\n      从 limitation 转化为 confirming evidence。temporal trend 增加 policy impact framing。\n      Limitation 段落诚实报告：无 ground truth depth annotation for CC data，\n      correlation 是 indirect evidence。best 档下审稿人接受此为 \"compelling supporting analysis\"。\n\n  - name: \"exp-028: Subsampling Power Curve\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-028\"\n    description: >\n      从 exp-001 (Pythia C4) 和 exp-017 (Qwen-cont C4) 的 30K 样本池中，\n      以 n∈{500, 1000, 1500, 2000, 2500, 3000, 4000, 5000} 做 10 次随机重采样，\n      每次计算 1v2 AUC 及 bootstrap CI，记录 K*=2 判定成功率（CI lower > θ=0.60）。\n      绘制 power curve，确定 80% 和 95% power 的最低样本量。\n    expected_results:\n      models_tested:\n        - Pythia-1.4B (1v2 AUC ≈ 0.6539, strong signal)\n        - Qwen-cont (1v2 AUC ≈ 0.6112, marginal signal)\n      resamples_per_n: 10\n      power_pythia:\n        n_500: 0.3\n        n_1000: 0.6\n        n_1500: 0.8\n        n_2000: 0.9\n        n_2500: 1.0\n        n_3000: 1.0\n        n_4000: 1.0\n        n_5000: 1.0\n      power_qwen_cont:\n        n_500: 0.1\n        n_1000: 0.3\n        n_1500: 0.4\n        n_2000: 0.6\n        n_2500: 0.7\n        n_3000: 0.8\n        n_4000: 0.9\n        n_5000: 1.0\n      ci_halfwidth_by_n:\n        n_500: 0.023\n        n_1000: 0.016\n        n_1500: 0.013\n        n_2000: 0.011\n        n_2500: 0.010\n        n_3000: 0.009\n        n_4000: 0.008\n        n_5000: 0.007\n      critical_n_80pct_power:\n        pythia: 1500\n        qwen_cont: 3000\n      critical_n_95pct_power:\n        pythia: 2000\n        qwen_cont: 4500\n      k_star_stability:\n        all_n_geq_2000_pythia_kstar_2: true\n        all_n_geq_4000_qwen_cont_kstar_2: true\n      key_finding: >\n        Pythia (strong signal) achieves 80% power at n=1500, 95% at n=2000.\n        Qwen-cont (marginal signal) needs n=3000 for 80%, n=4500 for 95%.\n        Our n=5000 design provides >95% power for all models including the most marginal.\n        CI half-width at n=5000 is ~0.007, sufficient to resolve AUC differences of 0.015+.\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下 power analysis 回应两个 reviewer concern：\n      (1) \"样本量够吗？\" → n=5000 对最强 signal (Pythia) 过饱和，对最弱 signal (Qwen-cont) 刚好充分。\n      这解释了为什么 Qwen-cont 的 CI lower=0.6015 如此边缘——它确实是 power-limited 的 marginal case，\n      但整体 7/8 的 evidence chain 不依赖这一个 configuration。\n      (2) \"最低需要多少样本？\" → n≥2000 对 moderate-to-strong signal 已足够，\n      这为 practitioner deployment 提供 actionable guidance。\n      CI half-width 的 1/√n 缩放与理论预期一致。\n      审稿人看到 power curve 后会认为实验设计是 well-powered 的，\n      Qwen-cont 的边缘性是 signal weakness（text-intrinsic）而非 design flaw。\n      这与 \"marginal case 不削弱整体结论\" 的核心辩护策略一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: K*=2 Detection Power by Sample Size\"\n        content: |\n          | n | Pythia (AUC≈0.654) | Qwen-cont (AUC≈0.611) | CI half-width |\n          |------|-------------------|----------------------|--------------|\n          | 500 | 3/10 (30%) | 1/10 (10%) | ±0.023 |\n          | 1000 | 6/10 (60%) | 3/10 (30%) | ±0.016 |\n          | 1500 | 8/10 (80%) | 4/10 (40%) | ±0.013 |\n          | 2000 | 9/10 (90%) | 6/10 (60%) | ±0.011 |\n          | 2500 | 10/10 (100%) | 7/10 (70%) | ±0.010 |\n          | 3000 | 10/10 (100%) | 8/10 (80%) | ±0.009 |\n          | 4000 | 10/10 (100%) | 9/10 (90%) | ±0.008 |\n          | 5000 | 10/10 (100%) | 10/10 (100%) | ±0.007 |\n      - name: \"Table: Critical Sample Sizes for K*=2 Determination\"\n        content: |\n          | Power Level | Pythia-1.4B | Qwen-cont | OLMo-1B (interpolated) |\n          |------------|------------|-----------|----------------------|\n          | 80% | ~1,500 | ~3,000 | ~2,000 |\n          | 95% | ~2,000 | ~4,500 | ~2,800 |\n          | 99% | ~3,000 | ~5,000+ | ~3,500 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Power curve — x-axis: sample size n, y-axis: fraction of resamples yielding K*=2. Two curves (Pythia solid, Qwen-cont dashed). Horizontal reference lines at 80% and 95%. Vertical drop-lines at critical n values. Shows our n=5000 is well above both 95% thresholds.\"\n      - \"Fig: CI half-width convergence — log-log plot of CI half-width vs n, with 1/√n reference line. Demonstrates that empirical convergence matches theoretical rate.\"\n    analysis: >\n      power analysis 将 Qwen-cont 的边缘性从 weakness 转化为 understood and quantified phenomenon：\n      AUC=0.611 距 θ=0.60 仅 0.011，需要 n≥3000 才能 robustly resolve。\n      我们的 n=5000 设计 provides adequate power，但 marginal signal 的存在本身\n      反映了 continuation mode 下 depth signal 确实更弱（vs rewrite 的 0.696）。\n      Power curve 同时为 practitioner 提供 deployment guidance：\n      如果只需要 binary detection (0v1)，n=500 即绰绰有余（AUC>0.92 everywhere）；\n      depth discrimination 的 power requirement 与 K* boundary 处的 signal strength 成正比。\n\n  - name: \"exp-026 arXiv Filtering Negative Result Integration\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_026_arxiv_filtering_integrated\"\n    description: >\n      将 exp-025 (Pythia filtering null) 和 exp-026 (arXiv graduated filtering null) 的负向结果\n      整合进论文 Section 5 和 Discussion。不产生新实验数据，但重新框架化已有结果，\n      引出 \"K* characterizes discriminability, not data utility\" 的核心洞察。\n    expected_results:\n      # 复用已有数据，无新实验\n      exp025_summary:\n        pythia_binary_vs_nofilter_mmlu_delta: \"+0.0017\"\n        pythia_binary_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_delta: \"+0.0000\"\n        pythia_graduated_vs_nofilter_mmlu_delta: \"-0.0007\"\n        conclusion: \"all deltas within noise (max 0.17pp)\"\n      exp026_summary:\n        arxiv_graduated_vs_nofilter_mmlu_delta: \"+0.0001\"\n        arxiv_graduated_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_delta: \"-0.0001\"\n        arxiv_binary_vs_nofilter_mmlu_delta: \"-0.0023\"\n        arxiv_binary_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_delta: \"+0.0042\"\n        conclusion: \"graduated ≈ no_filter; binary shows metric-specific trade-off\"\n      paper_framing:\n        section_5_addition: \"Table 5: arXiv Domain Filtering Results (K*=3)\"\n        discussion_insight: >\n          K* characterizes the statistical discriminability boundary of recursive generation depth,\n          not the downstream utility boundary. Depth 2 and 3 arXiv text is statistically distinguishable\n          (2v3 AUC=0.64) but not necessarily detrimental to training (graduated ≈ no_filter).\n          This distinction is practically important: K* tells curators WHERE detection can\n          differentiate depths, but not WHETHER differentiation improves outcomes.\n        honest_negative_framing: >\n          We hypothesized that arXiv K*=3 would enable graduated filtering to outperform binary.\n          This hypothesis was not confirmed. The null result reveals a fundamental distinction:\n          K* measures discriminability, not utility.\n      reviewer_reception_prediction:\n        credibility_boost: \"+0.3 to +0.5 ARR points on soundness/presentation\"\n        trivial_concern_reduction: \"honest reporting of disconfirmed hypothesis reduces suspicion of cherry-picking\"\n        insight_value: \"K* ≠ utility distinction is a genuine conceptual contribution\"\n 